  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "2ddb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "GENERAL INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a9b72752-c1e8-46ee-bf46-01946664bd0b",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Major Specific Criteria This articulation agreement displays lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Cal State LA lower-division course numbers range from 1000 - 2999. Students are advised to seek advisement from a counselor when planning to transfer to CSU Los Angeles and refer to the University Catalog to learn more about this major and its features. Additional admissions criteria for the major can be found on the Major Specific Criteria campus website. Please note that admissions requirements can vary by term so check back to see if there are any changes.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 24px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">Major Specific Criteria</strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">This articulation agreement displays lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Cal State LA lower-division course numbers range from 1000 - 2999. Students are advised to seek advisement from a counselor when planning to transfer to CSU Los Angeles and refer to the </span><a href=\"https://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> to learn more about this major and its features. Additional admissions criteria for the major can be found on the </span><a href=\"https://www.calstatela.edu/admissions/major-specific-criteria\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Major Specific Criteria</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> campus website.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\"><em>Please note that admissions requirements can vary by term so check back to see if there are any changes.</em>&nbsp; </strong></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "2edb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "RESOURCES FOR TRANSFER STUDENTS",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26db6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Cal State Apply Cal State LA College of Arts and Letters College of Arts and Letters Advisement Center Degree with a Guarantee Department of Modern Languages and Literatures General Education Lower Division Courses University Catalog",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Cal&nbsp;State&nbsp;Apply</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Cal&nbsp;State&nbsp;LA</a><a href=\"https://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=70&amp;poid=31599\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/academic/al\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">College&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;and&nbsp;Letters</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/academic/al/advisementfaq.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">College&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;and&nbsp;Letters&nbsp;Advisement&nbsp;Center</a></p><p><a href=\"http://adegreewithaguarantee.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Degree&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;Guarantee</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/academic/mld\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Modern&nbsp;Languages&nbsp;and&nbsp;Literatures</a></p><p><a href=\"https://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/content.php?catoid=77&amp;navoid=11897\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General&nbsp;Education&nbsp;Lower&nbsp;Division&nbsp;Courses&nbsp;</a></p><p><a href=\"http://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">University&nbsp;Catalog</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "30db6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "DIVERSITY REQUIREMENT FOR CAL STATE LA GRADUATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "afdd7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The articulation information in Assist.org not only shows a link to the admission requirements (aka our Major Specific Criteria webpage) but also Cal State LA graduation requirements that may be completed at the lower-division level, prior to transferring to the University. The diversity requirement is a graduation requirement , not an admission requirement. The diversity requirement may be completed prior to, or after, transferring to the University. For the Cal State LA degree, students will be required to complete two courses (six units) certified as diversity courses, at least one focusing on issues of race and ethnicity and their intersectionality with other social categories that structure inequality in society. These courses can be completed either at the lower-division or upper-division level from among courses satisfying GE requirements. Please view the General Education agreements on Assist.org for the lower-division courses that will meet the Diversity (d) and Race &amp; Ethnicity (re) Requirements.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The articulation information in Assist.org not only shows a link to the admission requirements (aka our </span><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/admissions/major-specific-criteria\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Major Specific Criteria </a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">webpage) but also Cal State LA graduation requirements that may be completed at the lower-division level, prior to transferring to the University. The diversity requirement is a </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">graduation requirement</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">, not an admission requirement. The diversity requirement may be completed prior to, or after, transferring to the University. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For the Cal State LA degree, students will be required to </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">complete two courses (six units)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> certified as diversity courses, at least one focusing on issues of race and ethnicity and their intersectionality with other social categories that structure inequality in society. These courses can be completed either at the lower-division or upper-division level from among courses satisfying GE requirements.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Please view the </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">General Education </strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">agreements on Assist.org for the lower-division courses that will meet the </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Diversity (d)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> and </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Race &amp; Ethnicity (re)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Requirements.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "2adb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "Spanish, B.A.",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2bdb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 7,
      "content": "The undergraduate program in Spanish includes a major for the Bachelor of Arts and a minor for students majoring in other fields. The total number of units required for the Bachelor of Arts degree in Spanish is 120 units, of which 45 units are in the major. Consult with an advisor for the specific number of units required in all areas of the degree including GE and free electives. Prior to beginning the Bachelor of Arts program in Spanish, students must have completed the second year of college-level Spanish or demonstrate equivalent language competency as evaluated by the Department faculty. All students complete a Common Core of 24 units (all upper-division) and 21 units of electives, as follows. NOTE: Select a total of 21 units of electives from the following groups A-E, with at least 3 units in each of groups A, B, and C: A. Linguistics and Language B. Spanish Literature C. Spanish-American Literatures D. Miscellaneous Hispanic Themes E. Courses Taught in English",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;program&nbsp;in&nbsp;Spanish&nbsp;includes&nbsp;a&nbsp;major&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;and&nbsp;a&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">minor</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;for&nbsp;students&nbsp;majoring&nbsp;in&nbsp;other&nbsp;fields.</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The&nbsp;total&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;units&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;Spanish&nbsp;is&nbsp;120&nbsp;units,&nbsp;of&nbsp;which&nbsp;45&nbsp;units&nbsp;are&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.&nbsp;Consult&nbsp;with&nbsp;an&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;specific&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;units&nbsp;required&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;areas&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;degree&nbsp;including&nbsp;GE&nbsp;and&nbsp;free&nbsp;electives.</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;beginning&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;program&nbsp;in&nbsp;Spanish,&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;have&nbsp;completed&nbsp;the&nbsp;second&nbsp;year&nbsp;of&nbsp;college-level&nbsp;Spanish&nbsp;or&nbsp;demonstrate&nbsp;equivalent&nbsp;language&nbsp;competency&nbsp;as&nbsp;evaluated&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;Department&nbsp;faculty.</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">All&nbsp;students&nbsp;complete&nbsp;a&nbsp;Common&nbsp;Core&nbsp;of&nbsp;24&nbsp;units&nbsp;(all&nbsp;upper-division)&nbsp;and&nbsp;21&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;electives,&nbsp;as&nbsp;follows.&nbsp;</span></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">NOTE:&nbsp;&nbsp;Select&nbsp;a&nbsp;total&nbsp;of&nbsp;21&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;electives&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;following&nbsp;groups&nbsp;A-E,&nbsp;with&nbsp;at&nbsp;least&nbsp;3&nbsp;units&nbsp;in&nbsp;each&nbsp;of&nbsp;groups&nbsp;A,&nbsp;B,&nbsp;and&nbsp;C:</strong></p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;Linguistics&nbsp;and&nbsp;Language</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;Spanish&nbsp;Literature</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;Spanish-American&nbsp;Literatures</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;Miscellaneous&nbsp;Hispanic&nbsp;Themes</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(137, 58, 171);\">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;Courses&nbsp;Taught&nbsp;in&nbsp;English</strong></p>"
    }
  ],
